+  them for `node_modules/todomvc-common/base.css` etc. referenced from the template.
+
+## Voyage 2: Browser-acceptance defects
+
+### Defect: DOM element identity loss on render
+
+An external browser acceptance suite reports 5 failures against the current production
+code. All share one root cause: the `render()` function in `js/app.js` sets
+`todoList.innerHTML = ''` and rebuilds every `<li>` element from scratch on each
+state change. A real browser holds element references across interactions; when the
+node is replaced, the reference detaches and Cypress errors with "element is no
+longer attached to the DOM".
+
+Affected acceptance tests:
+- "Mark all as completed" — toggle-all click + cy.eq() chain
+- "Clear the complete state of all items" — same pattern
+- "Mark items as complete" — individual toggle click + cy.find() chain
+- "Un-mark items as complete" — same pattern
+- "Hide other controls when editing" — toggle visible during editing
+
+The fix is app-side: mutate existing `<li>` nodes in place (toggle the `completed`
+class, set `checked` on the checkbox) instead of re-rendering the whole list.
+The `render()` function also needs to preserve element identity for toggle-all,
+clear-completed, editing save/cancel, and route filter changes.
+
+### Secondary defect: missing todomvc CSS in index.html
+
+The `index.html` omits `<link>` references to `todomvc-common/base.css` and
+`todomvc-app-css/index.css` that the template requires. The editing-visibility
+rule (`.editing .toggle, .editing .destroy { display: none }`) lives in
+todomvc-app-css, so the toggle stays visible during editing in a real browser.
+
+### Spec additions
+
+4 new scenarios added under a new "Rule: DOM element identity" block:
+1. `Clicking a completion toggle mutates the existing todo li element`
+2. `Toggle-all mutates existing todo li elements in place`
+3. `Unchecking toggle-all mutates existing completed li elements`
+4. `Double-clicking a label hides the toggle and destroy controls`
+
+These scenarios require step definitions (QM/Crew) that:
+- Capture `<li>` references before an action
+- Assert the captured reference remains valid and has the expected class/text after
+- Check computed visibility of toggle/destroy during editing
+
+### Watchbill
+
+`watchbill.json` has 8 watch groups including the new `dom-element-identity` group.
